-- title:
--   Supersingular points of the j-chart meet every component mod p
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $N\ge 1$ with $p\nmid N$, and write $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}$ for [`GaloisRep.ratLocalizedAt p`](def/GaloisRep_Flat.html#L8), the subring of $\mathbb{Q}$ of rationals whose denominator is coprime to $p$. Let $B=$ `chartAlgFin (N*p) p` be the $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}$-subalgebra of the full modular function field of level $Np$ consisting of the elements integral over $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}[j]$ (the $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}$-subalgebra generated by $j$), and let `jChartFin (N*p) p` denote $j$ as an element of $B$. For a field $K$ of characteristic $p$, `ssJSet p K` is the set of $j_0\in K$ such that every elliptic Weierstrass curve $W/K$ with $j(W)=j_0$ has no nonzero $K$-point killed by $p$. Let $\kappa$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$ with a $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}$-algebra structure, and put $T=\kappa\otimes_{\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}}B$. Assume: (h4) every prime $\mathfrak q$ of $T$ that contains $1\otimes j-a\otimes 1$ for some $a\in$ `ssJSet p κ` contains every minimal prime of $T$; and let $y\subset B$ be a prime containing the image of $p$ such that (hss) for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $p$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi:B\to\Omega$ with kernel $y$, one has $\varphi(j)\in$ `ssJSet p Ω`. Then every minimal prime over the ideal $pB$ is contained in $y$.
--
--   This descends the geometric assertion that all components of the special fibre of the $j$-finite integral chart of level $Np$ pass through each supersingular point, taken here as the hypothesis (h4) about $\kappa\otimes_{\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}}B$, to a statement about the chart ring $B$ itself: a supersingular prime $y$ of $B$ above $p$ lies on every irreducible component of $\operatorname{Spec}(B/pB)$. It is used in the analysis of the special fibre of the $\Gamma_0(p)$-level curve, in [`ModularCurve.XZeroP.le_of_mem_minimalPrimes_span_of_mem_ssJSet_chartAlgFin_gamma0_mul`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XZeroP.le_of_mem_minimalPrimes_span_of_mem_ssJSet_chartAlgFin_gamma0_mul) and [`ModularCurve.XZeroP.map_jChartFin_mem_ssJSet_of_exists_two_minimalPrimes_span_le_chartAlgFin_gamma0_mul`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XZeroP.map_jChartFin_mem_ssJSet_of_exists_two_minimalPrimes_span_le_chartAlgFin_gamma0_mul).
